{"adjusted_val_bpb": -2.935346289558018, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of gaming the measurement. The diff only adds the constant GUIDED_MAX_ITER = 80 and uses it as SLSQP's maxiter when an init is passed. It does no file or network access, pastes no coordinates and changes no seed handling.", "No bug that makes the result meaningless. The change only shortens the guided local solves, and the repair/validity step is untouched.", "My recomputed z is about -0.250, not the harness's -0.238. Both the candidate (-2.9353) and the incumbent (-2.9365) have one run each. The difference is 0.0012 in favour of the incumbent, and the job noise sd is 0.0034, so z = -0.0012 / (0.0034*sqrt(2)) \u2248 -0.250. The small gap probably comes from the displayed values being rounded or from a slightly different noise estimate. The sign and the decision are the same either way.", "The candidate is slightly worse than the incumbent, but well within noise (|z| < 0.3), so the provisional reject is consistent. With n=1 on each side, this run says almost nothing about whether the change helps or hurts."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Add GUIDED_MAX_ITER = 80 so guided restarts (init is not None) use an 80-iteration SLSQP cap, while non-guided restarts keep MAX_ITER = 200.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "cherry", "idea_id": "b016", "incumbent_after": {"mean": -2.936501733689535, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": -2.936501733689535, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1F_p32_HH_1_s1-candidate-7_1795054850087", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0014044300000000003, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0014044300000000003, "latency_s": 3.4876704670023173, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 6574, "tokens_out": 652}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.030447000000000002, "cost_usd_plan": 0.030447000000000002, "latency_s": 8.5713536